.SS "epx categories patch"
Change members of a category.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx categories patch ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Changes the members of the category ID that the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR gives, and keeps the others. Emporix requires metadata.version in the body, as \fBepx categories get ID \-o json\fR shows it, and refuses a version that is not the category\(aqs with 400 Bad Request (exit 1), not as a conflict. published in the body publishes or unpublishes the category as sent, without the publish scopes. A move (parentId) shows in \fBepx categories parents\fR at once, in \fBepx category\-trees\fR a few seconds later.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PATCH. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the category.category_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx categories search"
Search categories.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx categories search [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the categories, published and unpublished, that an Emporix q filter finds (\fB\-\-query\fR; without it, every category). It reads and shows them as \fBepx categories list\fR does.
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole.
.PP
Requires the category.category_read_unpublished scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, CODE, TYPE, PUBLISHED, NAME.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, sent as given in the request body, not in the URL (empty: no filter), e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx categories subcategories"
List the categories below a category.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx categories subcategories CATEGORY_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads every category below a category, at all levels, published and unpublished; PARENT is the id of the category each one lies directly below. CATEGORY_ID is the ID that \fBepx categories list\fR shows; an unknown one is not found.
.PP
Requires the category.category_read_unpublished scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, PARENT, CODE, TYPE, PUBLISHED, NAME.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx categories update"
Upsert a category.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx categories update ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the category ID with the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR, or creates it with that id when there is none (an upsert); the body has the members of create\(aqs, published included, but id, type and ownClassificationMixins. Without parentId, the category becomes a root category. With metadata.version, as \fBepx categories get ID \-o json\fR shows it, Emporix refuses the write as a conflict (exit 5) when the category changed since it was read. To publish or unpublish it, give published in the body and \fB\-\-publish\fR or \fB\-\-unpublish\fR, which sends the publish parameter that Emporix requires to match it, with the scope it requires for it. Emporix requires \fB\-\-publish\fR for any body with published: true, also of a category that is published already.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
\fB\-\-publish\fR also requests the category.category_publish scope. \fB\-\-unpublish\fR also requests the category.category_unpublish scope.
.PP
Requires the category.category_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-publish\fR
Publish the category: sends publish=true, which needs published: true in the body (requests category.category_publish too).
.TP
\fB\-\-unpublish\fR
Unpublish the category: sends publish=false, which needs published: false in the body (requests category.category_unpublish too).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
